Z||000000||FIERO1985||09-29-2001||05:36 PM||||Just to refresh my memory how to do a fuel pressure test is how?<P>I 1. Hook up pressure tester<BR>then do I crank it? do I need to pull any fuses or keep it from starting and what pressure reading should I get for the 2.8?<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||samoht||09-29-2001||06:11 PM||||i think it is around 28 to 32 PSI @ idle .. you are thinking of cylinder compression test where you disable the injectors and crank it 3 times.. I run around 40psi @ idle on my 3.2.. if you start to go to high your injectors will float.. Accel makes a variable fuel regulator, I think around 40 bucks.. but I have heard that a stock '85 will only make around 36 psi at idle max.. I put a corvette pump in mind.. does hook straight up though..||||reg||1
